!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-pin-on-a-dependent-field-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2"
  description: """
    A dependent field carries no pin, for the reason it carries no default: its type is not fixed at its declaration.
    A pin belongs on the sibling, which fixes the dependent field's type instead. A dependent type is also a type
    written in place that is no reference, and only a field typed by an atom, an enum or a reference carries a value,
    so the pin is refused on either ground.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
